  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_014 (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, and the only image encoder tested so far is resnet50, which alone achieved only 0.328 acc (config_003). The multimodal gain over RNA-only was modest (+0.028). Uncertainty: we do not know whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) can meaningfully increase the image modality's contribution or whether resnet50 is already near the ceiling for what image features can add. This experiment (config_002) is a clean single-variable swap from config_014—only the image encoder changes from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l—so any performance difference isolates the effect of image representation quality. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it tests a fundamental, unexplored design axis (image encoder capacity) that could either open a high-performing direction (if ViT-L substantially improves fusion) or confirm that image features are a minor contributor (allowing us to focus remaining budget on aggregation, fusion, or profile settings with the best RNA encoder)."
}

